Description
In this topic we will only describe the object Method as such, reserving the description of the programming
language SimTalk for the SimTalk Reference.
You can build your own routines using a combination of built-in methods, Keywords, assignments, and
control structures in the Method. Also check if one of the built-in Templates meets your needs. If this is
not the case, you can write your own templates for your use and for sharing them with your colleagues.
This construct combines productivity and flexibility. You can modify the behavior of an object, so that it
exactly fits your modeling needs, by writing user-defined methods. The built-in properties of the objects,
the large number of built-in methods provided, and the inheritance strategies help build valid models in a
short amount of time.
The Copilot can assist you in writing your source code in a Method.
You can access the functions of the Method on the Edit Ribbon Tab and on the Tools Ribbon Tab of the
Method.
You can select preferences for the Method Editor under File > Preferences > Editor.
Note
You can specify the settings that Plant Simulation applies when calling Methods during the simulation
runs under File > Model Settings/Preferences > Simulation > Methods.
The Method and user-defined attributes of data type Method have their own random number stream
which you can set with the attribute RandomSeed. As you are used to from the material flow objects,
Plant Simulation automatically assigns the random number stream when you insert an object, so that each
object has its own random number stream.
You can show the return value of a Method in an HtmlReport, compare Display a Method.
To show a tooltip with information about the Method, hover with the mouse over it.
