Calling a Method
You can call a Method you wrote in a number of ways. Either directly, by clicking Run or by calling it
Method from another Method.
Remarks
You can call a Method:
• By clicking Run 
  on the Tools ribbon tab in the Method window. You have to click Apply Changes
 first if you made changes to the source code. Pressing F5 and then F7 does the same.
If the Method expects parameters to be passed, Plant Simulation opens the Debugger where you type in
the parameters. You mainly use this way of calling a Method while developing your simulation model.
• By a call from a control from within another object. An Entrance Control in a Track object may, for
example, trigger a Method when a MU enters.
• By a call from another Method. This only works if the name of the Method is known. If the Method is
located in a different namespace, you also have to type in the Path to that Method.
• By a call from the EventController. The call &method.executeIn(time) will start the designated
Method after the time in seconds designated by the parameter of data type time has elapsed.
• By calling a reference. If a variable of data type object contains a reference to a Method, you type in
&Variable.execute.
Example
Method1                  // same namespace
root.Frame2.Method1      // path and name
&Method1.executeIn(8.5)  // pass to EventController, execute Method1 after 
8.5 seconds
Variable.execute         // call the referenced Method, note that the
                         // object Variable has the data type object
