Colors for Syntax Highlighting
Plant Simulation highlights elements in the source code in different colors according to their meaning.
Color in
source code Description Example
Black Designates normal source code.
Medium
green
Designates a comment you added to the source code.
Medium
blue
Designates a SimTalk function.
Purple Designates a keyword in SimTalk.
Brown Designates a value of data type string.
Medium red Designates an outdated function that is no longer
supported.
Compare Outdated SimTalk Names.
Gray blue Designates a deprecated function which is outdated and
should not be used.
It is currently supported for backward compatibility, but it
might become unsupported in the future.
