Working with Breakpoints
To work with breakpoints in the Method window, click the buttons on the Tools ribbon tab of the
Method or select the respective context menu commands.
Remarks
Proceed as follows:
• To insert or to delete a Class Breakpoint, click in the area of the row markers and breakpoints with the
middle mouse button or the mouse wheel.
To delete all class breakpoints, click Delete All Class Breakpoints.
• To insert or to delete an Instance Breakpoint, hold down Shift and click in the area of the row markers
and breakpoints with the middle mouse button or the mouse wheel.
To delete all instance breakpoints, click Delete All Instance Breakpoints.
• To activate the breakpoint contained in a line of source code, hold down Ctrl and click the middle mouse
button or the mouse wheel. Instead, you can also press Ctrl+F9.
• To open the dialog Breakpoint Settings, press Ctrl+B.
• To show a tooltip for a breakpoint, drag the mouse pointer over it and hover.
The tooltip always shows if the respective breakpoint is inactive.
Working with Breakpoints
